' Example: multi-agent handoff sequence.
' Agents are NEUTRAL participants — color belongs only to outcomes
' (Security FAIL red, Security PASS green, Cheek HOLD amber, packet blue)
' and to Cheek's human authority (purple). Color never carries status
' alone: every outcome states its literal word.
' Render from any directory — the include below is resolved relative to
' THIS file, not the plantuml launch directory:
'   plantuml -tsvg docs/plantuml/examples/agent-handoff-sequence.puml

@startuml verdant_agent_handoff_sequence
!include ../style.puml

title Agent handoff pipeline to Cheek

actor "Cheek" as Cheek <<human>>
participant "Grok\nResearch" as Grok
participant "Claude\nSpecs" as Claude
participant "Codex\nBuild" as Codex
participant "Security" as Sec
participant "Gemini\nQA" as Gemini
participant "Council" as Council

Grok -> Claude: HANDOFF research evidence
Claude -> Codex: HANDOFF implementation-ready spec
Codex -> Sec: HANDOFF slice + tests + SHA
alt Security FAIL
  Sec -[#C62828]-> Codex: <color:#B71C1C>**FAIL** — stop-ship</color>
  hnote over Sec #FFCDD2: <color:#B71C1C>Security **FAIL** outranks\nevery other green</color>
else Security PASS
  Sec -[#2E7D32]-> Gemini: <color:#1B5E20>**PASS** — HANDOFF for QA audit</color>
  Gemini -> Council: HANDOFF release-risk view
  Council -[#1565C0]-> Cheek: <color:#0D47A1>**CHEEK_APPROVAL_PACKET**\none recommendation + single next_slice</color>
  alt Cheek approves
    Cheek -[#2E7D32]-> Council: <color:#1B5E20>**APPROVE** & merge</color>
  else Cheek holds
    Cheek -[#EF6C00]-> Council: <color:#8A2C00>**HOLD / CHANGES_REQUESTED**</color>
    hnote over Council #FFE0B2: <color:#8A2C00>**HOLD** — evidence gap named,\nowner assigned, no merge</color>
  end
end

legend right
  |= Color |= Outcome (never a role) |
  | <#FFCDD2> | Security FAIL / stop-ship |
  | <#C8E6C9> | Security PASS / APPROVE |
  | <#FFE0B2> | Cheek HOLD / CHANGES_REQUESTED |
  | <#BBDEFB> | approval packet / process input |
  | <#F3E5F5> | Cheek — human authority |
endlegend

note over Cheek
  Sole ship authority — see AGENTS.md
  and docs/agents/HANDOFF_PROTOCOL.md
end note

@enduml
